# Surfy Chats Sheet

::summary
The Surfy chat-history sheet (F-13), anchored to the Surfy panel header's Chats button: the active conversation first (accent-selected), older chats with the fin glyph + last-activity meta and a trailing Delete, then the New chat row under the separator. Resume swaps the panel thread; the panel's grounding chip re-derives from the resumed chat's context.
::

::modal[name=surfy-chats title="Chats" width=340 placement=anchored anchor=surfy-panel dismissible=true]

:::row[icon=surfy-fin state=current action=resumeChat href=#]
Feature-union design round
Active now
:::

:::row[icon=surfy-fin action=resumeChat href=# trailing-label="Delete" trailing-action=deleteChat]
tidepool zip export ideas
Aug 03
:::

:::row[icon=surfy-fin action=resumeChat href=# trailing-label="Delete" trailing-action=deleteChat]
DMARC verification steps
Aug 01
:::

:::row[icon=doc action=newChat href=#]
New chat
Start a fresh thread
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. Chat rows carry the fin glyph (the bare accent Surfy fin, no chip or circle — the panel-header treatment at row scale). This file is the ONLY definition of the sheet — `shell.surf` references it by name and carries no inline copy. Stable name `surfy-chats` (matches this file's stem) for the backend wiring session; the panel-header Chats button's verb is `openSurfyChats`.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
